# Mirrors .gitignore, and that is the whole point.
#
# The verification image builds from a COPY of this directory, so anything
# excluded here is absent from the container exactly as it would be absent
# from a fresh clone. That is what makes `docker compose run verify` a
# clean-room check rather than a rerun of the maintainer's own tree.
#
# Keep this in step with .gitignore. If the two drift, the container stops
# being a faithful stand-in for a clone and the check quietly loses its value.
# `bb docker:verify` compares them and fails if they disagree.

.idea
*.iml
.cpcache
.nrepl-port
.claude
.cljs_node_repl
node_modules/
out/
**/.clj-kondo/.cache
example/*/.clj-kondo
.lsp
.clojure-mcp/
mcp-toolkit.jar
target/
_site/

# Not in .gitignore, because git handles these itself.
.git
.superpowers
.review
.review2
